| P12 | API Client Send has no live completion status | Compact `role="status"` region with request name, response code and duration; JSON body outside the live region | Round 16 finding |
| P13 | Tenant switch with an open applied key review leaves disclosure open | Any review exit, including switch, finalises disclosure | Round 16 finding; invariant I6 |
| P14 | Applied injection-override examples show "Not demonstrated" in the Playground | Topic examples classify under the topic key with a profile-aware verdict | Round 16 finding |
| P15 | Import from v1 is a separate destination | Also offered on the wizard tenant step as a secondary action; credentials re-entered via the secret sheet | First run is where an upgrading user needs it |
| P16 | Harness lifecycle 2 (mcp) reads an AES endpoint inventory (`CONVOS.mcp.tool` = `aes-inventory/get_endpoints`) and its follow-up is an AES policy review | The fixture reads the workspace MCP server inventory the core already exposes (`GatewayRead::McpServers`, C22) and the follow-up opens a Gateway guardrail review (`ChangeKind::GatewayGuardrails`) | AES has no admitted service (P18); the lifecycle stays read-only as in the prototype |
| P17 | Wizard tenant step requires a management OAuth client id and secret (`ERR.clientId`, `ERR.secret`) and makes the scan key optional (`scanOn`) | First run requires the scan key and makes the management client an optional second section; add mode keeps both optional. Secrets enter only through the host secret sheet | D013 (scan-key-first; management credentials are separate and never imply scan authentication) |
| P18 | Six products are verified, inventoried and administered (AIS tool policies, AES discovered AI and policies, AES policy review `REVIEWS.aes`) | Only products with an admitted service are verified, inventoried or changed: Runtime Security (`ManagementResource`, `ChangeKind`), Gateway (`GatewayRead`, Gateway `ChangeKind`s), Red Team and Model/skill reads (C13, read-only). Agentic Identity Security and Agentic Endpoint Security render as "Not available in this release" with their dependency gate; no inventory, verification result or mutation is invented for them | The existing interfaces do not supply those product APIs; fixtures cannot establish a capability (parity matrix, C13 rule) |
| P19 | Wizard Academy step creates a local account with streaks, reminders and a quiz (`s.acad`, `s.af`, `s.streaks`, `s.remind`, `s.quiz`) | The step signs in to the hosted Academy identity or skips; the embedded learner view owns progress and gamification | D004–D006, C04 |
| P20 | Key rotation issues a new key with a 24-hour grace period, a later revocation and a secret recoverable from the Keychain (`REVIEWS.key`, `keyRotated/keySecretClosed/keyDeployed/keyDoneAt`) | Two admitted operations in sequence: `ApiKeys · Version` (additional key, one-time reveal through the existing `RevealSecret` host sheet, never persisted) → local deployment acknowledgement → `ApiKeys · Delete` of the old key with readback. Two distinct timestamps; a lost secret means "issue another key" | `changes.rs` 842–846 and `management.rs` 980–988 define Rotate (regenerate, no grace) and Version (additional key); DESIGN.md "Secrets" forbids persisting issued keys |
| P21 | Test Cases "Run" was described in the first spec draft as scanning any case | Runtime-only "Open in Playground"; "Inspect" for every other product, which never dispatches a scan | Prototype lines 1035–1037 and the parity matrix (no invented execution) |
| P22 | Red Team Targets tab lists target names (`rtm` tables) | Targets shows `target_id` and `target_type` only | The C13 contract (`red_team.rs` 5–8, 56–66) deliberately keeps target names out of the core's reads; the privacy boundary is not widened for presentation |
| P23 | One rotation flow for every key | Staged Version → Delete rotation for Runtime API keys only; Gateway keys use `Rotate` (regenerate in place) | `gateway_changes::allowed` admits Rotate, not Version, for Gateway keys |
| P24 | Minimum window 1180×720 (DESIGN-V2 §4, tokens.md) | The host keeps `min_inner_size(900, 600)` until C34 because C01-N09 (re-run cumulatively by C24-N06) pins the legacy minimum; the v2 shell is laid out to stay usable without horizontal scroll at 900×600 (rail collapsed to icons below 1280 CSS px) and C28-N07 asserts it at that size. C34 raises the minimum together with the legacy-script retirement | Legacy native acceptance must keep passing while both shells exist (D058 §5) |
| P25 | Revision of P1/P2: "secrets enter only through a host secret sheet" | The retained, reviewed entry path (C02/C09) is a webview password field read through a ref, cleared immediately and sent once inside the intent as `EnteredSecret` (zeroized, never in React state, never logged); the host owns the *reveal* sheet (`RevealSecret`) and the clipboard. C29 uses exactly this path for the scan key, management secret and Gateway key; no new host entry sheet is built | The C27 spec assumed an entry sheet the host does not have; the reviewed pattern already satisfies D014 and the C24 canary checks (no secret in any AX tree or file) |
| P26 | `verifyTenantSetup` as one core intent streaming `VerifyStep`s (wizard.md) | The verify step issues one existing admitted read per line from the presentation (`management · verify`; the scan line reports the stored key's state; Gateway prerequisites run in Administration once a workspace is chosen) and shows each result as it settles | The core already authorises every read individually (D014); a new orchestrating intent would duplicate that authority for sequencing alone. Recorded in C29; revisit if a server-side verification endpoint is admitted |
| P27 | Add-tenant Cancel writes nothing except an already-vaulted credential | A tenant is created at the tenant step (credentials need a context) and the sheet makes it the active tenant at once so its credentials attach to it, not to the tenant the shell showed; Cancel after that keeps the tenant and any credential (and leaves it active), and the sheet says so; Cancel before it writes nothing | The retained core attaches credentials to an existing tenant |
| P28 | Gateway workspace key entered on the wizard tenant step | The step explains that the workspace key is configured in Administration › AI Gateway after a workspace is read (`selectGatewayWorkspace` must precede `configureInferenceCredential`) | The admitted sequence needs a workspace list read with a management client first |
| P29 | "Import from v1" fills the tenant step in place | The action navigates to the existing reviewed import destination (C23) | The import review flow is itself reviewed and must not be duplicated inside the wizard |
| P30 | The wizard opens whenever onboarding is not done | The shell shows onboarding as done whenever a tenant already exists (an upgrade, or a tenant created before the v2 shell was chosen); the stored state is untouched. A first run is one with no tenant yet | Existing users must never be sent through a first-run wizard (C28's native acceptance configures tenants in the legacy shell first) |

P10–P14 are the five round-16 Codex items carried as known gaps (see
[DESIGN-V2.md](DESIGN-V2.md) "Known gaps"). P16–P21 were added after the C27
attempt-01 review (R3–R6); P22–P23 after attempt-03 (F3a, F3b); P24–P25 were recorded in C28 and P26–P29 in C29 when implementation met the host as it is.
# C28 — Tokens, v2 shell behind the flag, Home skeleton

Phase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C27 and C26.

## Outcome

The new shell (sidebar with tenant switcher, navigation inventory, native shortcuts, palette, toasts, modal stack, theme) renders behind a Rust-owned `ui_variant` flag with a Home skeleton, and the legacy shell is untouched.

## Inputs and dependency gates

C27 specification. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),
[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).
Read the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its
companions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is
an immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.

## Milestones

1. `ShellSnapshot.ui_variant` and `onboarding` fields; `FeatureId::{Home, Inbox}`; one navigation inventory (label, shortcut index, sidebar membership, availability) consumed by the native menu, sidebar and palette; `navigate` intent; ts-rs regeneration.
2. `apps/desktop/src/styles/tokens.css` per tokens.md; `data-theme` from the observed appearance; no inline colours.
3. Shell components: sidebar (collapsing below 1280px), tenant switcher (switch intent only; guard dialog deferred to C30 but the refusal type is defined), palette, toast system (kinds, expiry, Reduce Motion persistence), modal stack with aria-hidden siblings, Home title row and read-status line placeholder.
4. React root switches on `ui_variant`; legacy shell unchanged; existing feature views mount inside the new shell as-is where they already exist.
5. Fixtures for boards R2Palette, R2Tenants, R2Dark; copy.ts for the shell.

## Required acceptance

- Invariants I8, I9, I10 with tests V2-T09, T10, T11 and native checks V2-N03, N04, N05.
- Minimum window 1180×720; no horizontal scroll at 1180 wide at 200% zoom.
- T09 native keyboard/focus/accessibility checks for every changed UI; the four accessibility additions in DESIGN-V2 §8 are in `native-checks.json` for C28.
- Screenshot evidence set at 100% and 200% in both themes under `evidence/C28/screens/`.

## Evidence and completion

Controller runs, native record, screenshots, Codex review (D034: may complete at 8 with no blockers; raised to 9 before P09 review).

## Safety and recovery

Flag defaults to `legacy` in the production identity until C34; fixture identity may default to `v2`.
