1:# Prisma AIRS Desktop v2 selected architecture draft
2-
3-All four candidates were selected by the owner on 2026-10-16. These are concrete
4-implementation recommendations for that selection, not application source or a
5-claim that G01 has passed. Product constraints D001–D023 remain unchanged.
6-
7-## Module ownership
8-
9-| Module | Owns | Does not own |
10-|---|---|---|
11-| Rust application core | Tenant/context admission, request coordination, configuration reviews, remote outcomes, protected work | Hosted grading or raw editor keystrokes |
12-| Tauri native host (desktop-host) | Window/origin/schema IPC admission, permission manifest/CSP, native Keychain/AppKit sheet/pasteboard adapters and process bootstrap | Domain review policy or hosted learning truth |
13-| React presentation | Immediate input/undo, layout, accessible controls, navigation and redacted state | Stored credentials, execution permissions, request settlement |
--
74-workspace/grant for Gateway, issuer/learner account for Academy, or project/
75-conversation/grant for Harness/MCP, with applicable native generations. Academy
76-scope is independent of tenant selection. Rust checks it at admission and dispatch claiming. A delayed tenant-A Scan cannot
77-silently use the newly selected tenant B, and A→B→A never revives an old reference.
78:CreateTenant has a validated nonsecret profile draft and no inherited credentials;
79:the host creates its ID/context before separate scan-key configuration. Cancel
80-binds the original operation and principal rather than whichever tenant is current.
81-
82-The wire envelope carries a native-issued delivery-session nonce and a string-
83-encoded u64 sequence. This is transport deduplication, not authorization or a
84-ContextRef. The typed facade serializes admission calls (not operation completion)
85-and advances sequence after the admission result. Native admission maintains an
86-O(1) high-water mark per principal/delivery session, retains all unsettled receipts
87-within queue bounds and the latest 256 settled admission results/input digests.
88-An identical retained duplicate returns the same result; changed input is refused.
89-An older evicted sequence is AlreadyProcessed with no dispatch, never a fresh
90-request. Gaps are refused without advancing. Refusals consume their accepted
91-sequence too, so ambiguous delivery cannot retry against changed authority.
--
162-Implemented in `crates/desktop-core` (`scanning`, authority `Scan` /
163-`CancelScan`), `packages/desktop-contracts` (validators) and
164-`apps/desktop/src/features/runtime`.
165-
166:- **Input.** `Scan { context, draft }` carries an explicit AI security
167-  profile (by name, at most 100 UTF-16 units on one line, or by UUID), the
168-  prompt and/or response and an optional application name (at most 256
169-  characters), exactly v1's four inputs. Working v1 (74754c02, read-only)
170-  caps a scan at 96 KiB of prompt plus response (`bridge/src/runtime.ts:193`,
171-  `src/input.rs:396,554`) and has no context, file or other large-input path,
172-  so the registered limits (2 MiB per text; escaped request plus a 16 KiB
173-  envelope allowance within the 8 MiB SDK request ceiling) cover every
174-  working v1 input without staged payloads. Admission re-validates and
175-  refuses `InvalidInput`; the presentation checks the same limits first. The
176-  React form is uncontrolled: values are read from the DOM when Scan is
177-  pressed, never pre-captured or stored.
178-- **Admission** requires the current context and a ready scan credential
--
408-  retries) and per-request `with_retries(0)`.
409-
410-## Fresh editor input and Configuration review
411-
412:React owns immediate editor text/undo; Rust owns captured immutable drafts and
413-review validity. Do not round-trip every keystroke through Rust to redraw text.
414-A fresh full editor snapshot is captured synchronously in the production Review,
415-Apply, Save and Send handlers. It carries raw validity, document identity and
416-input content; a debounced cached revision alone is insufficient. Invalid or
417-lossy input is refused without overwriting controls or claiming a faithful save.
418-
419:Review captures/validates/normalizes the fresh draft in Rust and stores an opaque
420-review record bound to application session, tenant, credential revisions,
421-Gateway workspace if relevant, approved destination, resource/version, exact
422:normalized draft/action and expiry. Apply receives the review reference plus a
423-fresh editor snapshot for comparison. Rust constructs the outgoing operation
424:only from the stored reviewed draft, never replacement client payloads. Different
425-current input, invalid input, retired context/resource or expired review refuses
426-Apply. Review consumption and operation creation are atomic; duplicate delivery
427-returns the same operation only for the same native-bound invocation and input.
428-A different invocation cannot reuse the consumed review, even after failure.
429-
430-RequestApply validates the fresh snapshot and opens a native operator confirmation
431-showing Rust's stored review summary/target. Its accept/deny callback is private
432-to the native host, session/review-bound and never serialized as a renderer
433-approval boolean/token. Recheck bindings after confirmation and before dispatch;
434-context changes while the dialog is open invalidate it. The host actively ends
435-the NSWindow sheet on retirement, not only when its callback arrives. First-reveal
436-expiry also ends the secret sheet, clears its plaintext accessory and zeroizes
--
458-refused while confirming. Denial retires that confirmation nonce without sending;
459-another attempt requires fresh capture/confirmation. Late/duplicate callbacks
460-cannot consume it again. Confirmation holds a modal editor/document lease: main
461-input, navigation and document replacement are disabled; a captured/programmatic
462:draft change invalidates the lease. Revalidate at callback. Native tests exercise
463-pending-dialog edits, not only typing before RequestApply. The native dialog's
464-stored operation summary remains the explicit authoritative action shown to the
465-operator; no claim is made that Rust can inspect arbitrary renderer-only text.
466-
467-Re-read the target baseline before a reviewed mutation and use conditional
468-resource/version preconditions where the actual endpoint supports them. Without
469-server-side compare-and-set, an external writer can still race the final read;
470-do not promise atomic remote conflict prevention. Preserve that limitation,
471-readback/reconciliation and exact known/unknown outcome semantics.
472-
473-Typing after Review makes it obsolete for the new input. Fresh capture at Apply
474-catches changes that have not reached a debounce or host capture; production
475-UI tests must exercise that exact race. Rust cannot independently prove what a
476-compromised renderer visually displayed: window admission and content binding
477-are enforced native rules, while faithful user-input capture is a tested
478-presentation contract. A renderer-supplied 'operator: true' is never sufficient.
479:Harness proposals enter captured drafts but cannot provide operator Apply.
480-
481-## Tauri contract and admission
482-
483-Use named host commands `desktop_dispatch` and `desktop_observe`, with finite
484-versioned wire unions; no generic shell/filesystem/HTTP/Keychain plugin grants.
485-Only the packaged main WebView may call them. Commands validate the native
486-window identity and allowed local origin as well as schema/version/size limits;

